# Build outputs
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
publish/

# IDE / tooling
.vs/
*.user

# Claude Code agent worktrees — ephemeral, created and torn down per background
# agent, never meant to be committed.
.claude/worktrees/

# graphify — entirely rebuildable, local CPU work only (no LLM, no network for
# --code-only, ~25s cold / ~1-2s incremental). Community IDs reshuffle on every
# cluster-only run even with no real change, so committing graph.json made every
# refresh a ~30MB, ~35%-churned diff — not worth it for a build that costs no
# tokens to redo. Rebuild per session instead (see CLAUDE.md's Graphify section).
graphify-out/

# The log loop's plaintext (LOG-LOOP-PLAN.md §6.1): the reader writes it under $TMPDIR/log-loop/ and
# refuses any path inside the repository; this is the second lock on the same door.
log-loop/
# …but the runbook folder is reviewed like code, so it is never ignored.
!.claude/log-loop/
